Narrow BOOLEAN syscall arguments at the PE/unix boundary.

Fork-local. NOT submitted upstream — see docs/upstream-status.md for what is and
is not established.

GetLogicalDrives() loops forever on this bundle: our llvm-mingw PE build writes
one byte of the `restart` argument slot, the System V unix side tests all 32
bits of it, and __wine_syscall_dispatcher forwards the slot raw. Stale garbage
above the low byte reads as TRUE, pinning the enumeration index at 0.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c
@@ -2073,6 +2073,16 @@
 }
 
 
+/* The PE side may pass a BOOLEAN with garbage in the high bits: the MS x64 ABI
+ * leaves them undefined, while the System V ABI this side is built for lets the
+ * compiler assume they were zero-extended.
+ */
+static inline int syscall_bool_arg( BOOLEAN value )
+{
+    return *(volatile unsigned char *)&value != 0;
+}
+
+
